---
// The generated side-rail stylesheet, emitted ONCE per page.
//
// Why generated and inline rather than a static .css file:
//   · A CSS `@media` condition cannot read a custom property — `@media (min-width: var(--x))`
//     is invalid — so the derived breakpoint has to be materialised as a literal SOMEWHERE.
//     Generating it from src/lib/sponsorLayout.ts keeps the arithmetic as the source of truth
//     and leaves exactly one place in the codebase where that pixel exists.
//   · YTT caution ②: shipping the CSS inside the SAME server-side conditional as the markup is
//     what makes a sponsors-off page carry no dormant site-narrowing rules. `railCss()` also
//     returns '' when there are too few sponsors for rails, so the fallback case emits nothing.
//
// CSP: §10.7 is `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'` — inline CSS is permitted (inline JS is not),
// so this adds nothing for audit-scripts to flag.
//
// Rendered near the TOP OF <body>, deliberately: it must come after the bundled stylesheets in
// <head> so that equal-specificity rules (`:root` redefining --container-max, `.wallMasonry`)
// win on source order, and early enough that the narrowing applies before content is painted.
import { railCss, railPlan } from '../lib/sponsorLayout';

const css = railCss(railPlan());
---

{css && <style is:inline set:html={css} />}
